<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Army of Flanders</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/flanders">Flanders</a> was the Spanish <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> army stationed in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/low-countries">Low Countries</a> from the sixteenth to the eighteenth century. It fought the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-revolt">Dutch Revolt</a> and other European wars and was one of the largest standing armies of its age. Supplied along the Spanish Road, it was a heavy financial burden on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-empire">Spanish Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/army-of-flanders.jpg" alt="Army of Flanders" width="320" height="234" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Terciosmarchando.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
